{"Cache key design creates stale data risk - key is realm + FetchMode but cached value multiplexes organization-specific results via searchKey (organizationId). Organization-to-IDP association changes (e.g., organizations().addIdentityProvider()) may occur independently without triggering registerIDPLoginInvalidation*, causing stale per-org subsets to persist": 0.7355861663818359, "Invalidation optimization is fragile to future changes - avoids invalidation when both old and new models satisfy getLoginPredicate() and orgId is unchanged, but this duplicates predicate semantics. If LoginFilter is extended with additional criteria beyond orgId/public logic, invalidation may not trigger unless updated in parallel, leading to stale cache": 0.12968546152114868, "Extending getLoginPredicate() with organization/public constraints at SPI level changes global semantics for all implementations, not just Infinispan cached provider. This couples organization visibility rules into generic SPI-level login filter and may cause behavior drift between existing callers and previous expectations for non-cached and custom provider implementations": 0.5150480270385742, "Added isEnabled() re-check signals potential inconsistency between getForLogin() contract and returned model state. The storage-provider level should guarantee getForLogin returns only currently enabled IDPs so presentation layers don't need to duplicate this safeguard": 0.4289567172527313}